  "mathematical_reason": "The genuine discounted-return model represents the absorbing physical cliff with a one-time penalty and then zero future reward. Finite-state Bellman inequalities bound every admissible history; the walk attains the true infinite return. At gamma9/10 the exact safe value from cell2 is1561/500=3.122, and the displayed difference -3.439+6.561 is exactly that value rather than3.12. The actual theorem2 expression using the exact value is -9049/4050, strictly negative and between-2.25 and-2.15, preserving the displayed approximate-2.2. The true global Bellman maximum and optimal-suffix induction separately show that every optimal history from any viable initial cell is safe for every nonnegative penalty, including p0. The proposal replaces only the erroneous exact equality and the rounded value inside the exact formula; it retains3.12 as the correctly rounded display. This is a narrow correction review, without whole49/exercise approval.",
